Generate dependency locks on Linux, and check on develop only

Armeria pulls in brotli4j, which picks its native binary via an
OS/architecture-activated Maven profile, so a lock written on a macOS arm64 host
records native-osx-aarch64 where the CI runner resolves native-linux-x86_64. The
first CI run failed on exactly that diff in the server and cli locks.

We ship a Linux image, so the Linux resolution is the one worth scanning. Make
that explicit: regenerate the locks in a container, and treat the ubuntu-latest
check as the authority on their contents.

Also drop main from the check's triggers -- it only receives merges from develop,
which has already gated the locks.

